* ============================================================================
* UNBLOCKED 2026-08-12, same session: the AIF-110 lane landed. Two defects
* fixed and runtime-proven on throwaway copies -- the rewrite loop's
* MISSING writeCurrent() (the actual blank-writer; every set() landed in a
* buffer the next appendBlank discarded) and the X64M identity stamped
* from the temp path stem (real, hex-verified, but NOT the blank cause).
* Long-name appends also landed en route (parse admits the x64 ceiling,
* descriptor gets the field_name_policy ~n token). Guard lifted.
* ============================================================================
* mcc_add_notes_memo.dts -- Part B of the AIF-070 memo-workspace plan (task
* #168; owner mechanism ruling 2026-08-12: "build the verb"). Adds NOTES M
* to the CANONICAL x64 STUDENTS and TEACHERS fixtures via FIELDMGR APPEND,
* then rebuilds their CDX+LMDB and re-saves the clean posture. The MCC
* rebuild chain (og -> x32 -> vfp -> x64) is untouched.
*
* This is v3 of the script; each earlier run bought a lesson:
*   run 1 (red): parseFieldSpec validates at its own tail, BEFORE append()
*     can resolve the memo flavor sentinel -- fixed in validateFieldDef.
*     Byproduct repair: re-saved posture attached students.cdx, which the
*     old canonical posture had silently omitted.
*   run 2 (mixed): appends SUCCEEDED (PB_T2/T4 green, 200/20 recs), but
*     (a) CDX containers are HASH-BOUND to table structure (reclen/fields/
*     hash in the tag directory) and correctly refuse the rewritten table
*     -- "CDX survives an appended column" was wrong, rebuild is REQUIRED;
*     (b) WORKSPACE OPEN DBF scanned the __fldbak backups in as areas and
*     the posture saved 15 areas -- backups must be gone before the save.
*
*   run 3 (red, two lessons): (a) CDX identity lives in a SEPARATE sidecar,
*     <container>.cdx.meta (cdx_meta.cpp) -- deleting only the .cdx leaves
*     the stale identity behind and the fresh container is judged by it;
*     (b) THE BIG ONE: fields_mgr's rewrite loop called gotoRec without
*     readCurrent, so every get() read a never-filled buffer and the
*     rewrite copied BLANK records (counts intact, values empty). Fixed to
*     match cmd_copy's loop, the prior art that always did both. The blank
*     tables were restored from the vfp lane -- the chain IS the backup.
*
* HOST PREREQUISITES (run before this script):
*   Remove-Item data\dbf\x64\STUDENTS.__fldbak.dbf, data\dbf\x64\TEACHERS.__fldbak.dbf
*   Remove-Item data\indexes\x64\STUDENTS.cdx, data\indexes\x64\TEACHERS.cdx
*   Remove-Item data\indexes\x64\STUDENTS.cdx.meta, data\indexes\x64\TEACHERS.cdx.meta
*   Remove-Item -Recurse data\lmdb\x64\STUDENTS.cdx.d, data\lmdb\x64\TEACHERS.cdx.d
*   (CDX CREATE refuses an existing container, and openCdx trusts the .meta
*   sidecar -- BOTH must go. The README's reset rule, now with its corollary.)
*
* KNOWN TWO-STEP (measured on the landing run 2026-08-12): FIELDMGR APPEND
* creates fresh <table>.__fldbak.dbf backups DURING this script, and the
* WORKSPACE OPEN DBF below scans them in -- so the first run saves a
* 15-area posture. After markers read green: host-delete the two fresh
* backups, then re-run ONLY the posture tail (WORKSPACE CLOSE / OPEN DBF /
* WORKSPACE / SAVE mcc_x64 / SAVE mcc_minidb_memo MEMO MINIDB / CLOSE) to
* land the clean 13-area posture and the 27-file container.
*
* Rerunnable: FIELDMGR APPEND refuses "already has a memo store" harmlessly
* once NOTES exists; the index rebuild and posture re-save still execute.
* NO MEMO VALUES ARE WRITTEN -- fixtures stay value-virgin (null tokens,
* empty sidecars). Writability is proven by workspace_minidb.dts DB_T3/T4.
*
* Markers:
*   PB_T1 STUDENTS freshness under REBUILT TAG SID (Taylor Quinn)
*   PB_T2 STUDENTS NOTES reads empty (null token)
*   PB_T3 TEACHERS readable under REBUILT TAG TID
*   PB_T4 TEACHERS NOTES reads empty
* Then: WORKSPACE must report 13 areas (backups gone), and the MINIDB
* container line must read 27 file(s) = 13 tables + 12 CDX + 2 DTX.
*
* Run: DO mcc_add_notes_memo   (fixture migration; not a regression)
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

DO x64
WORKSPACE CLOSE

FORMULA "MCC-NOTES-M-BEGIN"

* --- STUDENTS: memo column (no-op if already present) + index rebuild -------
SELECT 1
USE STUDENTS NOINDEX
FIELDMGR APPEND NOTES M
CLOSE

USE STUDENTS NOINDEX
CDX CREATE
CDX ADDTAG SID
CDX ADDTAG MAJOR
CDX ADDTAG LNAME
CDX ADDTAG FNAME
CDX ADDTAG DOB
CDX ADDTAG GPA
BUILDLMDB CLEAN YES
CDX TAGS
CLOSE

USE STUDENTS
SET INDEX TO STUDENTS
SET ORDER TO TAG SID
TOP
? "PB_T1_students_fresh_under_rebuilt_sid:" + (ALLTRIM(FNAME) = "Quinn")
? "PB_T2_students_notes_null:" + (NOTES = "")
CLOSE

* --- TEACHERS: same ----------------------------------------------------------
SELECT 2
USE TEACHERS NOINDEX
FIELDMGR APPEND NOTES M
CLOSE

USE TEACHERS NOINDEX
CDX CREATE
CDX ADDTAG TID
CDX ADDTAG DEPT_ID
CDX ADDTAG LNAME
CDX ADDTAG FNAME
BUILDLMDB CLEAN YES
CDX TAGS
CLOSE

USE TEACHERS
SET INDEX TO TEACHERS
SET ORDER TO TAG TID
TOP
? "PB_T3_teachers_readable_under_rebuilt_tid:" + (LNAME > "")
? "PB_T4_teachers_notes_null:" + (NOTES = "")
CLOSE

* --- clean posture re-save: WORKSPACE must report 13 areas ------------------
WORKSPACE CLOSE
WORKSPACE OPEN DBF
WORKSPACE
WORKSPACE SAVE mcc_x64

* --- the Part-B-meets-carriage proof: container must report 27 file(s) ------
WORKSPACE SAVE mcc_minidb_memo MEMO MINIDB
WORKSPACE CLOSE

FORMULA "MCC-NOTES-M-END"
